<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Dregovichs</h1><p class="st-meta">600 CE – 900 CE (approx.) · capital Turov</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An East Slavic tribe of the Pripyat marshes, whose lands around Turov later formed one of the principalities of Rus'.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Dregovichs settled the wet, forested lands between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pripyat-river">Pripyat</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-dvina">Western Dvina</a> in the 7th and 8th centuries. Their name is usually derived from a Slavic word for bog. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-vii">Constantine VII</a> mentions them as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/drougoubitai">Drougoubitai</a>, paying tribute to the Rus', in the 10th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They lived in small villages and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hill-fort">hill forts</a> and farmed the drier ground, supplementing this with hunting, fishing and beekeeping. The river <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pripyat-river">Pripyat</a> linked them to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> and to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a>, which made them early tributaries of the Kievan princes. The chronicle records that they had their own princely rule before Rus' control, but no names survive.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>By the 10th century the Dregovichs had been absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turov">Turov</a> became the seat of a princely line, and the territory developed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-turov-and-pinsk">Principality of Turov and Pinsk</a>. Their land is now southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dregovichs.jpg" alt="Dregovichs" width="320" height="244"><figcaption>Image: Лапоть · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jewellery_Dregoviches_GIM.jpg" target=